 I believe it is not Linux kernel problem, it's a firmware
(BIOS) bug.

 I have a Sony VGN-Z90S, one of a Japanse variant model of Sony VAIO
type Z series, perhaps mostly same as yours and I saw same reboot
problem.

 I've tried kbd/acpi/triple reboot....tracing kernel behaiver...
it is completely correct...but this machine hangs after console is
shutdown (backlight led is off after cleanly kernel shutdown process)

 But, after update the BIOS to version R2140M3 (provided at Sep 30
2008 in Japan. Sorry I don't have BIOS update information for other
country model..). The reboot problem is completely gone on the same
kernel.

 I recommed to you to update BIOS of your VAIO.

